From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, comctl32: SHObjectProperties shows the sheet; a drive's own General page

SHObjectProperties was a stub that returned TRUE and did nothing. File
Explorer calls it for the Properties of a drive in This PC, of search
results and of the folder it shows: none of them opened anything. It now
shows the properties sheet of a file, a folder, a drive or several files
(a double-NUL-terminated list; SHOP_FILEPATH, and SHOP_VOLUMEGUID by the
volume's drive), through the items' folder's "properties" verb, on a
thread of its own as Windows does (the caller goes on); SHOP_PRINTERNAME
opens the printer's properties (PrinterProperties).

A drive had no sheet even through the context menu: the data object of a
This PC item was asked of the desktop folder (a one-item folder taken for
the desktop), so no page came. It is asked of its own folder now, and a
drive gets a General page of its own (driveprops.c): its icon and label,
type (Local Disk, Removable Disk, CD Drive, Network Drive), file system,
used and free space with their bytes and size, capacity, a chart of the
two, and Disk Clean-up (cleanmgr.exe /d X, when the system has it). The
sheet is titled "Local Disk (C:) Properties".

Property sheets are titled "NAME Properties", as Windows titles them (not
"Properties for NAME").

Test: test/objprops-gate.sh with test/objprops-probe.c (mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_OBJECT_PROPERTIES in shellord.c, SG_MUTANT_NO_DRIVE_PAGE in
shlview_cmenu.c).
